        <briefdescription>
<para>Exact phrase search using positional index. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Tokenises <computeroutput>phrase</computeroutput> with the same whitespace tokeniser used during indexing, then returns documents where the terms appear as a consecutive run (pos[i+1] == pos[i]+1 for every adjacent pair). Results are BM25+-scored and sorted descending.</para>
<para>Edge cases:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Single-term phrase → equivalent to searchBM25.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Empty phrase → returns empty vector.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>phrase</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Raw phrase string. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>top_k</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Maximum results to return. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Ranked results, descending score. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
